{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1461470-catfish-procedure-spell","id":1461470,"title":"Catfish Procedure/Spell","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-25T20:18:48-07:00","id":1461470,"title":"Catfish Procedure/Spell","content":"In my story, a NWO Operative impersonates a Mage, Beatrice, who is in hiding, and then uses this guise to approach a Rhys, Mage from a different Cabal who has never met the real Beatrice, establishing a relationship. At the same time, she is communicating with Beatrice in the Digital Web, where both have projected virtual avatars(small a). She draws both Beatrice and Rhys into a scheme that both believe they stand to benefit from, but risks serious punishment by Tradition higherups if discovered. She wants to connect the two so that they carry on as if they had met and concocted the scheme all by themselves. Beatrice and Rhys both have Mind and have active Mind-Shields, preventing their memories from being altered. <br /> <br /> Instead of targeting either Rhys or Beatrice, the Operative wants to target the relationship between them, the conversation, so that it evolves in a way that obscures inconsistencies resulting from how they were set up. Entropy deals with the relationship between things and the probability of the conversation evolving in the desired way. Correspondence governs flow of information through space, spoken in person or sent as text on the Internet. Forces applies to sound, electricity and light - the Pattern Substance of the words as they travel. At high levels, Mind deals with the ideas that the words represent, independent of the speaker as they travel from one to the other.<br /> <br /> If this Catfish Procedure is even possible, what Spheres would be required and at what levels?<br /> <br /> Is it impossible? If so, why? <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T18:00:23-07:00","id":1461633,"title":"","content":"Entropy 5 can do the desired effect of altering &quot;a relatonship&quot; in abstract, bypassing mind-shields. 5 it's the level that explicitly deals with perfectly controling ephemeral/conceptual serendipity, you would be a bit limited by what's probable/possible but given time you should be able to mold the relationship as much as you want.<br /> <br /> Correspondence hardly does that (Data could <i>maybe </i>do something across these lines?). It's not the &quot;natural&quot; sphere to do any of this, it really doesn't govern &quot;information&quot; as much as &quot;the flow&quot; itself - the information usually needs to be informed (like, by Mind). Arguably Data isn't Information either - it's not Information until someone get's it (but if it's &quot;online&quot;, you can probably use Data, maybe also Correspondence, to &quot;intercept&quot; the conversation, and then alter it with a program or something). Even if it wasn't directly useful, you may end using this Sphere anyway just to deliver the effect from another place.<br /> <br /> Forces 3, of course, can alter the sound. Remember to both alter the sound and tackle physical conversational cues if they're in person. It's a valid option.<br /> <br /> Mind for this it's a bit iffy. It depends on what the ST thinks about the place of ideas/concepts in the cosmology and the limitations of Mind. Altering &quot;Ideas&quot; in such an &quot;Awakening Archmaster&quot; style to bypass a basic Mind shield might be either: Require a travel to the Astral Umbra to confront the Spirit of the idea / require Archspheres / Just require a big ritual and a lot of successes. It really depends on the ST, but I would say it isn't the &quot;natural&quot; Sphere to *not* have to deal with someone else's Mind shield, if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> There's a caveat with <i>directly </i>spinning countless spells arround two wizards to alter their conversation, and expecting no one to notice. Even w/o Prime they (or friends) could sense a <i>direct </i>supernatural manipulation with Awareness (and it's a Talent, so you could roll Perception even if no dots). They could be able to detect suspicious mojo it's working in the area. After all, they're Mages. Mages know things.<br /> <br /> If the comunication isn't direct, though, that's not such a big concern","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-26-2021, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T19:58:43-07:00","id":1461639,"title":"","content":"There's a subtle conversation technique whereby you implant an idea in someone's head in such a way that they think they came up with it themselves. In game terms, this would be a Manipulation+Subterfuge roll; a specialty such as False Innocence could help, too. On top of that, I'd allow Magick Enhancing Ability to lower the difficulty of this; probably a Mind Effect. This is on top of the Mind \u2022 capability to boost your own mental Attributes, which you'll want to do, too; you'll want your Manipulation as high as you can push it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-28-2022, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T12:11:22-07:00","id":1461742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1461470-catfish-procedure-spell?p=1461633#post1461633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entropy 5 can do the desired effect of altering &quot;a relatonship&quot; in abstract, bypassing mind-shields. 5 it's the level that explicitly deals with perfectly controling ephemeral/conceptual serendipity, you would be a bit limited by what's probable/possible but given time you should be able to mold the relationship as much as you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's perfect. My Operative is not powerful enough to have Entropy at five, but she could Requisition a Device that does it for this important mission. It only has to shape the conversation so that it avoids the two referring to how they came to know each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1461470-catfish-procedure-spell?p=1461633#post1461633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correspondence hardly does that (Data could <i>maybe </i>do something across these lines?). It's not the &quot;natural&quot; sphere to do any of this, it really doesn't govern &quot;information&quot; as much as &quot;the flow&quot; itself - the information usually needs to be informed (like, by Mind). Arguably Data isn't Information either - it's not Information until someone get's it (but if it's &quot;online&quot;, you can probably use Data, maybe also Correspondence, to &quot;intercept&quot; the conversation, and then alter it with a program or something). Even if it wasn't directly useful, you may end using this Sphere anyway just to deliver the effect from another place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking in combination with other Spheres, but Entropy 5 is simpler.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1461470-catfish-procedure-spell?p=1461633#post1461633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces 3, of course, can alter the sound. Remember to both alter the sound and tackle physical conversational cues if they're in person. It's a valid option.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's super tricky, because each has to be unaware that the other is seeing and hearing something different than what they are doing with their face and voice. An invisible screen between them with a supercomputer facilitating the alteration. One of the has Forces and would likely notice the effect cast so close to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1461470-catfish-procedure-spell?p=1461633#post1461633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind for this it's a bit iffy. It depends on what the ST thinks about the place of ideas/concepts in the cosmology and the limitations of Mind. Altering &quot;Ideas&quot; in such an &quot;Awakening Archmaster&quot; style to bypass a basic Mind shield might be either: Require a travel to the Astral Umbra to confront the Spirit of the idea / require Archspheres / Just require a big ritual and a lot of successes. It really depends on the ST, but I would say it isn't the &quot;natural&quot; Sphere to *not* have to deal with someone else's Mind shield, if that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am the ST. It occurs to me that the Operative could set one of them up with a reason to try to penetrate the other's mind-shield. If the two are engaged in a subtle contest of Mind Magick, the Operative could exploit the opportunity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1461470-catfish-procedure-spell?p=1461633#post1461633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a caveat with <i>directly </i>spinning countless spells arround two wizards to alter their conversation, and expecting no one to notice. Even w/o Prime they (or friends) could sense a <i>direct </i>supernatural manipulation with Awareness (and it's a Talent, so you could roll Perception even if no dots). They could be able to detect suspicious mojo it's working in the area. After all, they're Mages. Mages know things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither have Entropy, but one has Prime. If the targets are already seated together with the shared intention of having a conversation, the Device-powered Entropy 5 effect could shape that conversation to also be so engrossing that the Prime Mage ignores or doesn't even notice this single effect. The Operative has Arcane 3 and stealth if that makes a difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1461470-catfish-procedure-spell?p=1461633#post1461633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the comunication isn't direct, though, that's not such a big concern</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> She would want to have them meet in person. It would likely be at Rhys's home.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1461470-catfish-procedure-spell?p=1461639#post1461639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a subtle conversation technique whereby you implant an idea in someone's head in such a way that they think they came up with it themselves. In game terms, this would be a Manipulation+Subterfuge roll; a specialty such as False Innocence could help, too. On top of that, I'd allow Magick Enhancing Ability to lower the difficulty of this; probably a Mind Effect. This is on top of the Mind \u2022 capability to boost your own mentally Attributes, which you'll want to do, too; you'll want your Manipulation as high as you can push it.</div> </div> </div> </div>She has actually used this already on Rhys. He is the legal owner of a property where a Verbena Mage built his home in the deep woods over a century ago, the Verbena having outlived his real legal identity and having to entrust Rhys to act as the legal owners while he continues to live there. The Operative, posing as Beatrice, shares insider information about a company that leads Rhys to believe he could sell the property, buy some stock, sell the stock and then have more than enough money to buy the property back. When Rhys puts the plan together and proposes it, the Operative compliments him on his brilliance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":".  clarity 09-27-2021, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T21:15:23-07:00","id":1462071,"title":"","content":"Correction: Rhys doesn't have Mind. It suits the story better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}